.TH SMARTQUEUE 1
.SH NAME
smartqueue \- filter and display Slurm jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartqueue
.RI [ FILTERS ]
.br
.B smartqueue
.RI [ SQUEUE_OPTIONS ]
.br
.B smartqueue
.B --
.RI [ SQUEUE_OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Filters the current user's queue by directory, exact name, substring, regular expression, elapsed time, state, partition, stdin patterns, or latest matching job.
Combined filters are intersections.
.PP
Arguments not recognized as smartqueue filters are delegated unchanged to
.BR squeue (1).
Use
.B --
to force native mode when an option name overlaps with a smartqueue filter.
Native mode and smart-filter mode are separate invocations.
.SH FILTERS
.BR --this-dir ,
.BR --dir " " PATH ,
.BR --name " " NAME ,
.BR --contains " " TEXT ,
.BR --regex " " PATTERN ,
.BR --older-than " " DURATION ,
.BR --younger-than " " DURATION ,
.BR --time-left " " DURATION ,
.BR --state " " STATE ,
.BR --partition " " NAME[,NAME...] ,
and
.BR --latest .
.PP
.B --latest
does not add a state restriction.
StartTime is used when every candidate has one; otherwise the highest JobID is used.
.PP
.B --younger-than
and
.B --time-left
use strict less-than comparisons.
Non-numeric remaining-time values such as NOT_SET and UNLIMITED are excluded.
